## Claude Code

- The rules above are `~/.agents/CORE.md`; do not re-read it. Before file writes, multi-step tool work, delegation, current-fact research, Unreal Engine work, or judging models, renders or images by eye, read `~/.agents/ROUTER.md` and only the packs it selects. If a shared file is missing, continue with this block and say so.
- Subagents always get an explicit model; never launch a general-purpose agent without one. `heavy-output-runner` (sonnet): bulky read-only evidence gathering. `step-runner` (sonnet): one briefed step. `project-explorer` (haiku): project map. `claim-verifier`, `evidence-overseer` (opus): verification. Checklist sweeps: pass `model: haiku`. A hook may push back once on the model choice; re-issue the call unchanged to keep it.
- For wake-ups on a long job, arm `Monitor` (load it with ToolSearch) on the job's log with a filter for checkpoint and failure lines and the maximum timeout, and re-arm it on each expiry until the job ends.
- Put a script over a few lines, or one with backslashes or nested quotes, in a file with Write and run the file; inline heredocs and `-c`/`-e` strings lose backslashes and quotes. On Windows run Python with `-X utf8`, also next to `-I`, which ignores the `PYTHON*` variables.
- Before handing over a report, handoff, or design conclusion, run `verify-claims` on its mechanism claims (who calls, owns, or moves what); anything not Verified stays `Assumption:`. Once per document version: rerun only on claims that changed, never as a general double-check of your own work.
